## Domain Subindex System

{{DOMAIN_COUNT}} domain-specific index file(s). Each lists only the wiki pages relevant to that domain. Pages CAN appear in multiple domain indexes when they span domains.

{{DOMAIN_INDEX_TABLE}}

**Why this matters.** When an AI system or downstream consumer only needs content from one domain, it reads the relevant `domain-index-*.md` instead of the full index. That scopes the context without creating separate vaults. The Diagnostic Quick Reference in each domain index maps specific questions to answers — this is the primary retrieval affordance.

**Cross-domain pages.** A page that bridges two domains should be listed in every domain index where it's relevant. The page itself should have a `> **Cross-domain:** [...]` callout explaining the bridge.

